From: ps3 <ps3@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:36:26 +0300
Subject: irr OpenGL driver: fewer GL calls per draw (LU_GL switches)

LU_GL=0 turns everything below off, LU_GL_<name>=0 one of them.
UPLOAD: a new hardware buffer was uploaded twice (glBufferData, then glBufferSubData of the same bytes because the link's ChangedID was never set).
BIND: glBindBuffer for the buffer that is bound is left out and the buffers stay bound after a draw; drawing from client memory unbinds first.
XFORM: the view and world matrices go to GL as one glLoadMatrixf when the next 3D draw needs them, and a transform that changes nothing costs nothing.
PTR: the vertex arrays of a buffer are not set again for the next draw from the same buffer.
FOG: the same fog is not set again.

diff --git a/irr/include/LuGlOpt.h b/irr/include/LuGlOpt.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/irr/include/LuGlOpt.h
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+// Our PS3 package: switches for the changes that cut GL calls and uploads (docs in luanti/patches).
+// They are on by default; LU_GL=0 in the environment turns all of them off (the game as upstream
+// draws it), LU_GL_<NAME>=0 turns one off. Read once per call site (keep the result in a static).
+#pragma once
+
+#include <cstdlib>
+
+inline bool luGlOpt(const char *name)
+{
+	const char *all = getenv("LU_GL");
+	if (all && all[0] == '0' && !all[1])
+		return false;
+	const char *v = getenv(name);
+	return !(v && v[0] == '0' && !v[1]);
+}
+
+inline int luGlInt(const char *name, int def)
+{
+	const char *v = getenv(name);
+	return v && *v ? atoi(v) : def;
+}
